{"severity":"error","file":"errors/old_misuse_1.march","start_line":2,"start_col":22,"end_line":2,"end_col":32,"message":"`old(…)` cannot be used in an `@invariant`.","code":"old_misuse","fix":null,"labels":[],"notes":["`old(e)` means `e` of the state a message arrived with, so it is only meaningful in a handler's `ensures`: `on Msg(…) ensures state.n >= old(state.n) do … end`."],"category":"REFINEMENT"}
